{
  "comment": "Accelerator strings as Settings records them. `event` is the keydown (missing modifier flags are false; `keyCode` is the Windows virtual key, read only on Windows). `accelerator` is what `acceleratorFromEvent` (ui/src/lib/accelerator.ts) returns on each of `platforms`, or null when the recorder refuses the key; a doubled accelerator is the chord pressed twice, which ui/src/settings/ShortcutInput.svelte joins with a space on macOS. `parsed` is what the Rust parsers read from it: `macKeycode` for shortcut_check::parse (null: refused), `windowsVk` for keys::chord (null: refused), `canDouble` for double_press::parse of the chord written twice, `doubleKey` for double_press::parse of a doubled accelerator. `windowsKeyNames` pairs a virtual key with the name both `windowsKeyName` (accelerator.ts) and keys::name (src-tauri/src/keys.rs) give it. Read by src-tauri/src/accelerator_contract.rs and ui/src/lib/contracts.test.ts.",
